WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:05.978
A paint shop sells three base paints

2
00:00:05.978 --> 00:00:08.224
Meadow, Harbour and Brick.

3
00:00:08.307 --> 00:00:10.969
Each litre carries fixed amounts

4
00:00:11.052 --> 00:00:14.380
of three pigments, yellow, blue and red.

5
00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:16.569
A customer wants exactly

6
00:00:16.646 --> 00:00:19.558
five grams of yellow, fifteen of blue

7
00:00:19.558 --> 00:00:21.321
and twenty two of red.

8
00:00:21.321 --> 00:00:24.770
How many litres of each paint should we mix?

9
00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:27.835
Three unknowns at once is hard.

10
00:00:27.835 --> 00:00:31.162
Which unknown would you remove first

11
00:00:31.162 --> 00:00:33.351
and with which equation?

12
00:00:33.351 --> 00:00:34.840
Pause and think.

13
00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:42.897
Let x, y and z be the amounts of Meadow

14
00:00:42.897 --> 00:00:45.024
Harbour and Brick.

15
00:00:45.136 --> 00:00:48.158
Counting yellow gives two x

16
00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:51.180
plus y plus z equals five.

17
00:00:51.292 --> 00:00:54.650
Blue gives four x plus three y

18
00:00:54.762 --> 00:00:57.784
plus four z equals fifteen.

19
00:00:57.896 --> 00:01:01.478
Red gives two x plus four y plus

20
00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:04.500
eight z equals twenty two.

21
00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:08.329
The plan: use the first equation to remove

22
00:01:08.412 --> 00:01:10.400
x from the two below it

23
00:01:10.483 --> 00:01:13.133
then use the new second equation

24
00:01:13.216 --> 00:01:15.370
to remove y from the last.

25
00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:18.625
The two in front of x in the first

26
00:01:18.703 --> 00:01:20.906
equation is the first pivot.

27
00:01:20.906 --> 00:01:23.266
The blue equation has four x.

28
00:01:23.345 --> 00:01:25.626
Four divided by the pivot two

29
00:01:25.705 --> 00:01:27.750
gives the multiplier: two.

30
00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:31.746
Subtract two times the whole first

31
00:01:31.853 --> 00:01:34.748
equation from the blue one.

32
00:01:34.748 --> 00:01:37.858
Four x minus four x is zero

33
00:01:37.858 --> 00:01:40.645
three y minus two y is y

34
00:01:40.645 --> 00:01:44.184
and four z minus two z is two z.

35
00:01:44.184 --> 00:01:48.580
On the right, fifteen minus ten is five.

36
00:01:48.930 --> 00:01:51.730
So the blue equation becomes

37
00:01:51.830 --> 00:01:54.330
y plus two z equals five

38
00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:56.530
and it has no x left.

39
00:01:57.110 --> 00:01:59.398
The red equation has two x

40
00:01:59.398 --> 00:02:02.787
so its multiplier is two over two: one.

41
00:02:02.787 --> 00:02:05.668
Subtract the first equation once

42
00:02:05.753 --> 00:02:08.634
and the red equation becomes three

43
00:02:08.719 --> 00:02:11.430
y plus seven z equals seventeen.

44
00:02:11.780 --> 00:02:15.660
Now x appears only in the first equation.

45
00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:18.547
The bottom two equations

46
00:02:18.643 --> 00:02:22.777
now hold only y and z, so we can draw them.

47
00:02:22.777 --> 00:02:25.276
Across is y, and up is z.

48
00:02:25.276 --> 00:02:28.929
y plus two z equals five is one line

49
00:02:29.025 --> 00:02:32.005
and three y plus seven z equals

50
00:02:32.101 --> 00:02:34.120
seventeen is another.

51
00:02:34.470 --> 00:02:36.675
They cross at one, two.

52
00:02:36.675 --> 00:02:40.510
That point is the y and z we are after.

53
00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:44.357
The second pivot is the one in front

54
00:02:44.448 --> 00:02:47.443
of y in y plus two z equals five.

55
00:02:47.443 --> 00:02:50.257
The last equation has three y

56
00:02:50.257 --> 00:02:54.250
so the multiplier is three over one: three.

57
00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:57.697
Subtract three times the second

58
00:02:57.797 --> 00:03:00.094
equation from the last

59
00:03:00.094 --> 00:03:02.591
and watch its line turn.

60
00:03:02.591 --> 00:03:04.789
Three y plus seven z

61
00:03:04.789 --> 00:03:07.986
minus three times y plus two z

62
00:03:07.986 --> 00:03:09.484
leaves just z.

63
00:03:09.484 --> 00:03:13.080
And seventeen minus fifteen is two.

64
00:03:13.430 --> 00:03:16.535
The line ends up flat: z equals two.

65
00:03:16.535 --> 00:03:19.640
It turned about the crossing point

66
00:03:19.726 --> 00:03:22.573
because an elimination step never

67
00:03:22.659 --> 00:03:24.470
changes the solution.

68
00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:27.608
The system is now a staircase

69
00:03:27.693 --> 00:03:30.166
each equation has one unknown

70
00:03:30.251 --> 00:03:32.383
fewer than the one above.

71
00:03:32.383 --> 00:03:34.855
We call it upper triangular

72
00:03:34.855 --> 00:03:38.010
and its pivots are two, one and one.

73
00:03:38.590 --> 00:03:41.954
A common slip: subtract on the left side

74
00:03:42.038 --> 00:03:43.804
and forget the right.

75
00:03:43.888 --> 00:03:46.579
Then the blue equation comes out

76
00:03:46.663 --> 00:03:49.270
as y plus two z equals fifteen.

77
00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:53.106
On the picture that is a different line

78
00:03:53.106 --> 00:03:56.331
and it misses the answer completely.

79
00:03:56.331 --> 00:03:59.207
A step works on whole equations

80
00:03:59.207 --> 00:04:01.908
so the right side changes too

81
00:04:01.908 --> 00:04:05.220
fifteen minus two times five is five.

82
00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:09.234
And not every subtraction eliminates.

83
00:04:09.234 --> 00:04:13.318
Take the blue equation minus the first one

84
00:04:13.318 --> 00:04:14.339
just once.

85
00:04:14.431 --> 00:04:17.123
You get two x plus two y plus

86
00:04:17.216 --> 00:04:18.979
three z equals ten.

87
00:04:18.979 --> 00:04:22.320
That is true, but x is still there.

88
00:04:22.670 --> 00:04:25.264
The multiplier is not a guess.

89
00:04:25.350 --> 00:04:27.511
It is the entry to remove

90
00:04:27.598 --> 00:04:30.710
divided by the pivot: four over two.

91
00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:32.840
Back to the staircase.

92
00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:35.094
We solve it from the bottom up

93
00:04:35.094 --> 00:04:37.770
and that is called back substitution.

94
00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:41.804
The last equation says z equals two.

95
00:04:41.804 --> 00:04:44.259
Put it into the second

96
00:04:44.259 --> 00:04:48.557
y plus four equals five, so y equals one.

97
00:04:48.557 --> 00:04:51.115
Put both into the first

98
00:04:51.115 --> 00:04:54.901
two x plus one plus two equals five

99
00:04:54.901 --> 00:04:56.640
so x equals one.

100
00:04:56.990 --> 00:04:58.919
One litre of Meadow

101
00:04:58.919 --> 00:05:02.102
one of Harbour and two of Brick.

102
00:05:02.102 --> 00:05:04.128
Multiply back: five

103
00:05:04.128 --> 00:05:07.021
fifteen and twenty two grams

104
00:05:07.021 --> 00:05:08.950
exactly the target.

105
00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:12.831
So elimination comes down to three ideas.

106
00:05:12.911 --> 00:05:15.327
The multiplier is the entry to

107
00:05:15.407 --> 00:05:17.661
remove divided by the pivot

108
00:05:17.742 --> 00:05:20.318
and we subtract that many copies

109
00:05:20.398 --> 00:05:22.250
of the whole pivot row.

110
00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:23.640
Step by step

111
00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:26.200
the system becomes a staircase

112
00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:28.920
and no step changes the solution

113
00:05:28.920 --> 00:05:31.880
the line turns about the same point.

114
00:05:32.230 --> 00:05:34.926
Back substitution then solves the

115
00:05:35.008 --> 00:05:37.377
staircase from the bottom up.

116
00:05:37.377 --> 00:05:39.828
Each step divides by a pivot

117
00:05:39.828 --> 00:05:41.870
so no pivot may be zero.

118
00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:45.494
Each of our steps changed one row

119
00:05:45.586 --> 00:05:47.985
and left the others alone.

120
00:05:47.985 --> 00:05:51.490
That is exactly what a matrix can do.

121
00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:55.380
In part two we write each step as a matrix

122
00:05:55.380 --> 00:05:58.920
and see what happens when a pivot is zero.
